## Context

The author wants to see a working local website, not only plans or a project
encyclopedia. Implement a bounded first slice of 0726 and 0727 under tracker 0725.
Freeze existing evidence, export website-ready data, build country/project/method
views and useful aggregate visualisations. Add a sizeable, source-backed bundle
of historical closed energy operations from the four countries. Public deployment
and monthly operations remain in 0727/0728. Do not close the parent tickets.

## First test

A fixture with an undisclosed identity, a register-derived signature assertion,
a repeated financing observation and an operational event reported retrospectively
must export without inventing an identity, payment, signature date or backwards
chronology. A historical filter must exclude active and post-JETP approvals,
retain the source's closed status, and expose missing/invalid duration dates.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Reproducible offline export with input hashes, source links and coverage gaps
- [x] Homepage synthesises progress and country differences with attributable totals
- [x] Four country summaries, searchable catalogue, project timelines and methods/downloads
- [x] Historical closed energy-related operations with selection rules, source links and instrument filters
- [x] Static local preview and browser checks covering navigation, filters, aggregates, downloads and mobile layout
- [x] Gates run with failures and limitations reported; no acceleration or physical-completion inference from administrative closure

## Scope and dependencies

Uses the current documentary corpus and the Markdown-first storage contract.
This first slice does not require the complete historical matching study 0730,
full data-paper release, bulk Markdown dossier writing, or a SQLite service.
The first historical bundle is descriptive, including older and mixed-sector
operations with their sector/instrument labels. It is not a causal control group.

